<title>USA: Carrington Labs to buy back preferred.</title>
<headline>Carrington Labs to buy back preferred.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Carrington Laboratories Inc Thursday that it plans to repurchase 50 percent of its 330 outstanding shares of Series E convertible preferred stock.</p>
<p>The company said that the buyback comes in light of the firm's positive cash flow for the fourth quarter of 1996 and tha fact that it has over $10 million in cash on hand.</p>
<p>It said the plan will reduce the number of common stock shares issuable upon conversion.  The company will still have over $6 million in cash in the bank with no meaningful debt.</p>
</text>
